  "body": "#675 reminded me of an idea by @lukewagner that everything should be a module, somehow, so it'd be easier to use from WebAssembly. If that came to pass we'd probably need more granular `[SecureContext]` and `[Exposed]` annotations.\r\n\r\nIt might also make sens that inside a module we'd use `[AvailableIn]` rather than `[Exposed]` so that the latter can be reserved for truly exposing something on a global, whereas `[AvailableIn]` (bikeshedding welcome) would indicate where it's functional. E.g.,\r\n```webidl\r\n[AvailableIn=Window]\r\nmodule dom {\r\n  [Exposed=Window]\r\n  interface Node { ... };\r\n\r\n  ...\r\n};\r\n```",
